      "writtenOn": "2023-10-25T10:05:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wrong check: `\u003c#interrupt-cells\u003e` defines the number of cells **per interrupt** but `interrupts.len()` should be the number of interrupts (`.collect()` currently makes it the product of the two).\n\nTo illustrate, `/timer` has:\n```\ninterrupts \u003d \u003cGIC_PPI 0xd IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW\n              GIC_PPI 0xe IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW\n\t      GIC_PPI 0xb IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW\n\t      GIC_PPI 0xa IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW\u003e;\n```\ni.e. 4 interrupts with 3 cells per interrupt.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "fd2dadb62ceb33d7670445e7a0c5eeade8d032a4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67bfb216_e224716b",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/devices.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-25T10:05:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But `self` isn\u0027t `vm_dtbo` so consuming it doesn\u0027t help.\n\nFor example,\n```\n// vm_dtbo: \u0026mut Fdt\nlet info \u003d DeviceInfo::new_validated(vm_dtbo, fdt).unwrap().unwrap();\n// can\u0027t use vm_dtbo here as it\u0027s borrowed (good!)\ninfo.apply_overlay_and_patch(mut_fdt).unwrap();\n// can use vm_dtbo again as the borrower is gone (bad!)\n```\n\nAt the very least, this method should be `unsafe` although this is probably symptomatic of the OOP abstraction not being well encapsulated.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "fd2dadb62ceb33d7670445e7a0c5eeade8d032a4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
