      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T17:09:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can move this to ctor, but multiple loop is still required; Could you double check whether your suggestion is to remove loops?\n\nI need to iterate multiple times anyway because of the borrow checker. For example, when iterating `__symbols__`, I can\u0027t edit `FDT` because iterator keeps immutable references.\n\nI may fold loops for \u0027Clean up unused node and unused properties\u0027, and \u0027Clean up unsued symbols in __symbols__\u0027, but then getting `FdtNodeMut` in the loop looks tricky. Three options:\n\n- Option 1) call `vm_dtbo.node_mut(SYMBOLS_NODE_PATH)` whenever needed: Code will work, but I feel little bad because of unnecessary FDT traversals for getting the same node.\n- Option 2) (unsafe) keep the offset of the `__symbols__` node and use it to regain `FdtNodeMut` for editing `__symbols__` (aosp/2810553): Faster, but seems like a dark magic.\n- Option 3) Keep multiple loops\n\nI previously picked Option 3), but Option 1) seems to be your favorite. Could you share your opinion?",
      "parentUuid": "ceafe3ed_d3648871",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 216,
        "startChar": 8,
